  "description": "MUWLEX crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group I -4. Reported CIF formula moiety: C74 H104 Dy5 N8 O25 1+,3.5(H2 O1),Cl1 1-,5(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.500-3.651 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.26-99.52°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy5(LH)4(η1-Piv)(η2-Piv)3(μ2-η2η1-Piv)2(H2O)]Cl·9.5H2O·5MeOH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
